From: Claude (macro camera agent) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: gc5035: name the subdev after an optional DT label

The Galaxy A52 5G has two GC5035 modules (depth at 0x37, macro at 0x3f)
with different optics and tuning. libcamera derives the sensor model, and
from it the tuning file and sensor helper, from the part of the entity
name before the I2C address, so both load gc5035.yaml. Let an optional
"label" property replace the driver name in the entity name
("gc5035_macro 22-003f") so userspace can tell the modules apart.
Without the property nothing changes.

Applies on top of the depth agent's gc5035.c work in linux-sm7125.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c
@@ -1870,6 +1870,7 @@
 
 static int gc5035_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 {
+	const char *label;
 	struct device *dev = &client->dev;
 	struct gc5035 *gc5035;
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sd;
@@ -1941,6 +1942,13 @@
 
 	sd = &gc5035->subdev;
 	v4l2_i2c_subdev_init(sd, client, &gc5035_subdev_ops);
+	/*
+	 * Boards can carry several GC5035 modules with different optics and
+	 * tuning. Userspace (libcamera) derives the sensor model, and so the
+	 * tuning file, from the entity name, so let DT "label" rename it.
+	 */
+	if (!device_property_read_string(dev, "label", &label))
+		v4l2_i2c_subdev_set_name(sd, client, label, NULL);
 	sd->internal_ops = &gc5035_internal_ops;
 
 	ret = gc5035_initialize_controls(gc5035);
